[info title="Why prices matter"]
Prices act as *signals*. A rising price tells producers "make more" and
consumers "use less", reallocating resources without anyone issuing orders.
[/info]

## Key Takeaways

- Scarcity forces choice; every choice has an opportunity cost.
- Land, labour, capital, and entrepreneurship combine to produce goods.
- Demand and supply interact to determine market prices.
